able circumstances is not easy, especially, as it will be seen, for the higher pitches. Without mechanical appliances even good ears are deceived in the Octave. The differences of pitch noted by Helmholtz, Donders, Merkel, and Koenig, as given on p. 109d, probably point @@FN@@
